        "id": 2052731
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-27T21:58:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When I examined the `connection_streams`, I initiated and accepted two sockets using the same `connection_value`. This revealed that a single `connection_value` can be associated with multiple server sockets when executing more than one socket operation. Therefore, for `ReceiveData` and `SendData` methods based on connection_value, I used the most recently added socket object. This ensures that the socket handling data transmission is active.\n\nSimilarly, with `self.connection_server_sockets`, I observed that a `connection_value` can be linked to multiple listening socket objects. Hence, I\u0027ve treated the associated value as a list and appended new socket objects to it. For the `AcceptL2CAPChannel` method, I\u0027ll use the last socket added to this list, ensuring we\u0027re working with the most recent listening socket.",
      "parentUuid": "b998e041_c663530c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 210,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 210,
        "endChar": 56
      },
      "revId": "e0e8d4410383426be345acdf925303701aba6f8b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
